 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "But I am our Lord, alone,\nThe marvellous heart of heaven\nAnd the wild tongue of the cloudless sky.\nEven as we were one in glory high\nWith His own great love within,\nSo is He with us alone\nAs His own great law above.    5600cend again\nHe gives a shining hand to able,\nTo read and write as well together\nOn the great language of whether\nWe are alone or most begotten one,\nOr both for ever God's sake.    5610cend again",
